msgid ""
"Implementations not supporting the feature will treat keyed topics as "
"standard topics. The implications are explained throughout the tutorial. In "
"addition, endpoints using `Cyclone DDS <https://index.ros.org/p/"
"rmw_cyclonedds_cpp/>`_ will not even match with Fast DDS or Connext DDS "
"endpoints for this kind of topics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:50
msgid "Creating custom IDL messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:52
msgid ""
"ROS 2 users can define their own :ref:`custom topic "
"messages<CustomInterfaces>` in the ``.msg`` format. Then, the ROS 2 message "
"generation stack translates it to the DDS native `OMG IDL (Interface "
"Definition Language) <https://www.omg.org/spec/IDL/4.2/About-IDL>`_ message "
"format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:55
msgid ""
"One of the advantages of defining messages in IDL is the ability to use "
"annotations. Annotations are metadata to the data structure definition that "
"provide additional information about IDL constructs such as modules, "
"interfaces, operations, attributes, and data types. They are relevant for "
"code generation, documentation, or other purposes. Annotations in IDL "
"typically follow the ``@`` symbol and can be applied to various IDL "
"constructs. The ``@key`` annotation is used to designate a member as key, "
"which is covered in the following section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:61
msgid ""
"Users can define their own messages in the IDL format directly (following "
"the `ROS 2 interface design documentation <https://design.ros2.org/articles/"
"idl_interface_definition.html>`_) or use the ``msg2idl`` tool within the "
"``rosidl_adapter`` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:64
msgid "Creating Keyed Messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:66
msgid ""
"Keyed topics exist when one or more fields in the data structure are "
"annotated as keys. These key fields serve as unique identifiers for topic "
"instances in order to organize and manage the data samples, facilitating "
"efficient access, retrieval, and filtering of data based on the specified "
"key criteria."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:69
msgid ""
"The ``@key`` annotation designates a field as a key for the given topic "
"type, which can have zero or more key fields and can be applied to structure "
"fields of various types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:71
msgid ""
"Any primitive, such as booleans, integers, characters, strings or sequences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:72
msgid ""
"Other existing or defined messages. If those have defined an inner key "
"member, then those fields will we used as part of the key. Otherwise, the "
"key will be the concatenation of all the fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:76
msgid ""
"In order to specify multiple keys, separate ``@key`` annotations are used. "
"The following example shows how to define a keyed message using the IDL "
"format:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:79
msgid ""
"# KeyedMsgName.idl\n"
"module package_name {\n"
"  module msg {\n"
"    struct KeyedMsgName {\n"
"      @key long key;\n"
"      string data;\n"
"    };\n"
"  };\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:93
msgid ""
"Currently, the only supported message format that can be annotated with "
"``@key`` is *.idl*. Neither ``.msg`` nor ``.srv`` files support annotations "
"yet."
msgstr ""

